  "head_commit": "993771a98b8f39c7a83418d6b6da4182b8a3c797",
  "working_tree": "Modified source; the file digests below, not HEAD alone, identify the tested component implementation.",
  "schema": 18,
  "implemented": [
    "Connector::message_extension and deliver_observed opt into full normalized receipts; legacy deliver_attempt/deliver remain compatible.",
    "Worker::reconcile reads status under the original job ID without sending. Current original sender and route/delegate credential, membership and route authorization precede observation/replay; claim/dispatch still check task authority before any new effect. Receipt communication uses native current task assignment, so terminal-task answers are unassigned rather than rejected or resumed.",
    "Worker::observe accepts adapter-verified callbacks for normalized adapters. Projection, full receipt/event, actual reply source IDs and ordinary/task reply admission commit atomically; older acceptance cannot regress terminal delivery or lose an as-yet-uncommitted synchronous answer. Delivery-only SMS evidence remains recordable after STOP/lease expiry without changing policy; reply-bearing receipts and new dispatch retain current SMS eligibility.",
    "Worker::receive journals independently created adapter-authenticated contacts under a configured route with current policy before duplicate handling, payload/external binding checks and bounded durable receipts. Subsequent same-conversation replies reference the actual incoming message source.",
    "voice::Worker::with_observed_driver explicitly uses VoiceReceipt and durable reducer while retaining RemoteCall control capabilities. Builtin startup and with_driver retain the previous carrier dispatch path. Status of an owned physical effect continues after revocation without granting new mutations.",
    "Migration018 is additive, backup gated and included in snapshot digests. Exact schema17 backup transition retains installation, revocation and immutable manifests; older populated migration/rollback cases retain every original row."
  ],
